\title{The three units and the one data path}
\taxon{Card}
\tag{card}
\meta{anki}{1786395976741}
\meta{anki-deck}{MLSys}

\prompt{What are the three units inside a TPU [[OGCRQ]], and what is the data path from [HBM](AI2G) to compute?}{
  \ul{
    \li{\strong{[MXU](OGCRP)} — matrix multiply on a systolic array. Nearly all of the FLOPs.}
    \li{\strong{[VPU](OGCRN)} — elementwise ops (ReLU, add, mul) and reductions.}
    \li{\strong{[VMEM](GFK2)} — an on-chip scratchpad in the TensorCore, like L1/L2 but far larger (~128 MiB on v5e) and \em{programmer-controlled} rather than a cache.}
  }

  The path is HBM #{\to} VMEM #{\to} [VREGs](OGCRO) #{\to} MXU/VPU #{\to} VMEM #{\to} HBM. Nothing computes directly out of HBM. All of it is pipelined — the copies overlap with MXU work, so the array never stalls waiting on memory.
}
